# More moves in SVR Anthology PC: what blocks them and a plan

From Piloun1, 2026-11-07, for KaikoClanworth1 (svr-anthology-pc). Companion of `REQUEST_KAIKO_ANTHOLOGY_SLOTS.md`
(R5) and `BIG_ROSTER_ANTHOLOGY_PLAN.md`. Addresses are from a **static, read-only analysis of the SvR 2011 disc
program** (`Original\default.xex`, the base your Anthology build recompiles). Sizes were measured on my Anthology
(game + 14 DLC). Nothing of yours was run.

---

## 0. Short version

- Move ids are not the problem (3 283 used out of 32 767). **The Royal Rumble category banks are**: every added move
  must also go into `MOT\RR00` (strikes), `RR01` (grapples) or `RR02` (others), and in Anthology the last DLC's copies
  are already **17.3 MB (RR00) and 18.9 MB (RR01)**.
- The game does **not** have a fixed number of RR banks: it tries `MOT/RR00`, `RR01`, `RR02`, `RR03`… until one is
  missing, and gathers each wrestler's motions from **all** of them, one bank at a time. So new moves could go into
  **new banks (RR04, RR05…)** instead of growing RR00 / RR01: content only, no code change, to be confirmed in game.
- The "16 MiB per bank" rule is empirical (a Xenia test of mine, see 2.4). Anthology's 17-19 MB banks run without any
  memory change from Yumboy11 except pool 1 (32 -> 64 KB); the largest pool is 20 MiB. In your build, measuring the real
  headroom and raising a pool is cheap.
- Your Move Packs extend the stock banks (sorted insert), so they meet the same size wall, and their overlay mount
  (`sub_825953B0`, pacs' own tables) cannot read 13 of Anthology's pacs (see the slots request, R2 gotcha).

