## 2. How the game loads the RR banks (disc program)

### 2.1 The bank list — `sub_8224C4C8`
`sprintf("MOT/RR%02d", n)` for n = 0, 1, 2… while the entry exists (`sub_826A17D0`), then the same with `"MOT/RB%02d"`;
names go in a list of 16-byte slots (1 024 bytes cleared: **64 names** at most), count at +52. Any mounted pac can
provide a bank (the DLC overrides RR00-02, RR03 comes from `m.pac`). So `RR04` would simply be the next one found.

### 2.2 Building each wrestler's motion set — `sub_8224E180` -> `sub_8224CFD0`
`sub_8224E180` builds the list (2.1), then for each wrestler of the match allocates a 1 416-byte motion-set object
(`sub_8269A8D8(1416)`, or `sub_8269BA30(89)`) and constructs it with `sub_8224CFD0` (vtable 0x8200584C). The
constructor starts with the wrestler's own bank `"/MRR/%04d"` when `sub_8224CE20(this)` says so (that test reads match
settings, not whether the bank exists), else with `"MOT/RR00"`, and requests the load (`sub_826A2FA8`).

### 2.3 Gathering the motions — `sub_8224D8C8` (vtable +4, 0x82005850)
A state machine that walks the banks **one at a time** (counters at +100 for RR, +104 for RB): `sprintf`, exists,
load, then copies out of that bank the motions the wrestler needs (sorted list of at most **267** entries of 16 bytes,
`memcpy` = `sub_8269BC38`) into the wrestler's set. A motion is therefore taken from whichever listed bank holds it.

### 2.4 Sizes and memory
- Memory pools, table at 0x82DAC2F8 (`{id, size in KB}`), identical in 2011 and Anthology except pool 1: 0:4352,
  1:32 (Anthology 64), 2:12800, 3:5888, 4:12288, 5:8192, 6:2048, 14:5120, 7:2660, 8:1104, 9:1088, 10:6112, 11:4096,
  12:4608, 13:86, 15:350, **16:20480 (the largest, 20 MiB)**, 17-22:1024, 23-25:416, 26-28:1024, 29-34:600, 35-37:192,
  38:1280, 39:3072 (107.7 MB in all). Pool 0 (4.25 MiB) is the match load memory you raised to 16 MB in 2.1.9.
- The official 2011 DLC keeps RR00 / RR01 at 63 999 / 63 994 blocks of 256 bytes, just under 64 000 (16 384 000).
- My Xenia test on SvR 2011 (2026-10-31): added moves grew RR00 / RR01 from 16.37 MB to 17.7-18.4 MB -> AJ Styles
  crashed in match and moves that had worked became fallback finishers. Since then my tool keeps every bank under
  16 MiB - 64 KiB (16 711 680 bytes).
- Yet Anthology ships RR00 / RR01 at 17.3 / 18.9 MB and runs. So the limit is probably a pool (pool 16?) shared by the
  bank being read and what is gathered at the same time, not a per-bank constant (no 0xFA0000 / 16 MiB size constant
  found near this code).

## 3. Plan

### Step 1 — measure in your build (small)
Log, for each RR / RB bank load: name, size, the heap / pool it goes to and the free space left; and the size of each
wrestler's gathered set. Run a stock 30-man Royal Rumble in Anthology (DLC RR01 = 18.9 MB). This gives the real
headroom and tells which pool to raise.

### Step 2 — remove the wall (pick one or both)
- **2a. Raise the pool** (like A2, at start-up): the one found in step 1 (e.g. pool 16: 20 -> 64 MiB) and pool 0 to
  16 MB as in 2.1.9 (if the Anthology build does not have it yet). On PC this is cheap, and RR00 / RR01 can grow again.
- **2b. Extra RR banks**: confirm that `MOT/RR04` (in the last DLC's `m_dlc02.pac`) is listed and used: Piloun1's
  tool can write one added move that way (all its other parts as today: BMD0, MDL1, MOTP, WAZE, misc data, script).
  If it works, no bank ever has to exceed its size, and the 64-name list allows dozens of banks.

### Step 3 — wrestlers with their own bank (`mRR.pac`)
When `sub_8224CE20` sends a wrestler to `/MRR/<id>`, a move added to his moveset but missing from that bank is not
found (fallback finisher). Options: make `sub_8224CE20` return 0 for wrestlers whose moveset holds ids absent from
their MRR bank (or for every edited wrestler), or let the gathering continue into the RR banks after the MRR bank.

### Step 4 — Move Packs for Anthology (optional, bigger)
Today they grow the stock banks and rely on the own-table mount. For Anthology: build the overlays from the
`plist360.arc` sections (13 pacs have TOC headers that disagree with the .arc, listed in the slots request), and put
new moves into new RRnn banks instead of growing RR00 / RR01.

### Step 5 — tests (Piloun1 can run them, Xenia and your build)
1 added move, then 20, then 100: a normal match, a 30-man Royal Rumble (with an Anthology-added wrestler **and** a
2011 wrestler who has an MRR bank), the Create-a-Moveset preview (menu memory: the game's SPE1 +1 MB crashed), and
memory logs from step 1.

## 4. Numbers to keep
- Move ids <= 32 767: they are read as signed; 2K ids 34 007-60 355 crashed Create-a-Moveset on Xenia (2026-10-30).
- Ids used by the official DLC (your `dlc_move_ids.json`, 303 ids) must not be reused.
- Per wrestler: at most 267 gathered motion entries (`sub_8224D8C8`).
